  "surprise": "P25 wider residual, narrower MLP (d_model 384 -> 448, 8 heads of 56, d_ff 1280 -> 896; 9,770,880 params as registered) on 153-claude scored 688/677/662 on seeds 0/1/2 vs 676/700/685: exact means 675.67 vs 687.00, -11.33, paired +12/-23/-23, inside the registered -45..+40 but below its central +3. Discard. Mechanical predictions held: pretraining steps 4119/4096/4128 (mean 4114 vs 4503, -8.6%, inside 3,700-4,400 as the bench ratio 0.90 predicted), although the shape is only ~2% more matmul FLOPs per token, so 56-dim heads and (448,448) Newton-Schulz cost more than the MLP width they replaced; epochs 3.64/3.62/3.65. Final main val loss was LOWER, 0.0840/0.0809/0.0800 vs 0.0883/0.0869/0.0888 (minima 0.0767/0.0802/0.0741 at 150/240/270 s), and pretrain held-out greedy was 0.9705/0.963/0.962 vs 0.9675/0.967/0.968. The better-sampler mechanism failed anyway: round-1 targets solved 679/784/293 (mean 585 vs 153's 736, -21%; the registered falsifier < 450 did not fire on the mean, but seed 2 collapsed to 293 at sample acc 0.088), whole-run Lean parse failures 16.8/13.8/25.3% of 266,912 samples (153: 15.8/15.5/14.9%), both-ok samples 325,297 vs 353,098 (-7.9%). RL recovered most of it: round-4 RL-solved 1148/1148/1142 (mean 1146 vs 1172, inside the registered 1,120-1,210 but below 153 on every seed) with unchanged eval/round-4 transfer 0.599/0.590/0.580 (153: 0.584/0.599/0.575). Deep bins tied: >=10 110/106/104 (106.7 vs 107.7), >=11 25/23/25 (24.3 vs 23.7), >=12 6/3/3 (4.0 vs 4.3), L* 12/11/11. RL sampling 200-272 samples/s, totals 1770/1836/1745 s. Reading: lower pretraining val loss again did not buy RL (as in 150/155); residual width does not keep paying past 384 when the MLP is cut to 2x to fund it, or 153's +14.7 (all on seed 2) was partly luck. At the 10M cap, further capacity has to come from parameters the cap does not count (looping, pretraining-only modules like the MTP block) or from speed.",
